VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:4010
VITE_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:4010
VITE_INTERPOLATION_MS=12000

# Which backend `npm run static-data` reads route geometry and stops from when
# regenerating public/data/. Build-time only — the app itself never reads this.
# Falls back to VITE_BACKEND_URL, then to the dev backend above. Point it at a
# production backend when regenerating from a machine with no local .cache.
# STATIC_DATA_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:4010

# Unset, the basemap follows London's daylight: bright by day, dark at night.
# Set this to pin a single style — a self-hosted tile server, or an offline one.
# VITE_MAP_STYLE=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/positron

# --- Error reporting (src/error-reporting.ts) ---
# Both sinks are optional. With neither set, nothing leaves the device and the
# reporter is a console log — forwarding a user's errors to a third party is a
# privacy decision and, for the store builds, a disclosure one.
#
# CI supplies these from secrets; they are not set for local builds, and with no
# DSN the Sentry SDK constant-folds out of the bundle entirely rather than
# shipping ~30KB of dead code. Leave them commented out here.
#
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# The release the uploaded source maps are filed under. CI sets it to the git
# tag; a mismatch here means stack traces stay minified. Do not set by hand.
# VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=
#
# Plain-POST escape hatch, for anywhere Sentry is not wanted.
# VITE_ERROR_ENDPOINT=
